message:
I am thinking...: Now I understand the MLE header structure. The header fields are:
- `mSecuritySuite`: 1 byte (0 for k154Security)
- `mSecurityControl`: 1 byte (Mac::Frame::kKeyIdMode2 | Mac::Frame::kSecEncMic32)
- `mFrameCounter`: 4 bytes (little-endian)
- `mKeySource`: 4 bytes (big-endian, key sequence)
- `mKeyIndex`: 1 byte ((keySequence & 0x7f) + 1)
- `mCommand`: 1 byte (the command type, which comes after the header)

Wait looking again at the structure:

```cpp
uint8_t GetLength(void) const
{
    uint8_t rval = sizeof(mSecuritySuite) + sizeof(mCommand);

    if (mSecuritySuite == k154Security)
    {
        rval += sizeof(mSecurityControl) + sizeof(mFrameCounter) + sizeof(mKeySource) + sizeof(mKeyIndex);
    }

    return rval;
}
```

So GetLength() = 1 (secSuite) + 1 (command) + 1 (secControl) + 4 (frameCounter) + 4 (keySource) + 1 (keyIndex) = 12 bytes

For IsValid():
```cpp
bool IsValid(void) const
{
    return (mSecuritySuite == kNoSecurity) ||
           (mSecuritySuite == k154Security &&
            mSecurityControl == (Mac::Frame::kKeyIdMode2 | Mac::Frame::kSecEncMic32));
}
```

I need to look at what `kKeyIdMode2` and `kSecEncMic32` values are.

